From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:27:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Name throw sites for not-callable and null-base accesses

In a minified bundle the enclosing function name is usually "", so
"not a callable function" and "cannot convert 'null' or 'undefined' to
object" locate nothing. The Call* opcodes and to_object/base_class name
the callee type and the enclosing function, and the by-name and
by-value property opcodes raise V8-shaped "cannot read/set properties
of undefined (reading 'k')" errors that name the key. A computed key
is described without running user code. Every message is built in a
#[cold] #[inline(never)] helper on the throw path only, so it does not
enlarge the hot handlers.
---
